---
title: Institutional Goals and Objectives
summary: Our commitment to students and our goal of preparing Spirit-empowered Christian leaders.
---

# Our Commitment to Every GCUA Student

At Great Commission University of America, our commitment to every student reflects our mission, vision, and core values. We seek to develop spiritually mature, biblically grounded, academically equipped, and Holy Spirit-empowered Christian leaders.

## 1. God the Father

We encourage students to develop a close and personal relationship with God the Father, growing in the knowledge of His love, grace, and faithfulness.

## 2. Jesus Christ

We inspire students to deepen their devotion to Jesus Christ, submit to His Lordship, and reflect His character in every area of life.

## 3. The Holy Spirit

We encourage students to develop a deeper relationship with the Holy Spirit, recognize His guidance, obey His direction, and depend on His power for Christian living and effective ministry.

## 4. Humility

We seek to cultivate Christlike humility through the example of our faculty and staff, preparing students to serve others and glorify God rather than themselves.

## 5. Prayer and Intercession

We encourage students to develop a consistent life of prayer and intercession as an essential foundation for spiritual growth and effective ministry.

## 6. Biblical Knowledge and Learning Skills

We equip students with biblical knowledge, critical thinking, and practical skills for lifelong learning, sound interpretation of Scripture, and effective application of biblical principles.

## 7. The Church

We encourage students to love, support, and actively serve the Body of Christ, while remaining committed to their local churches and God's mission.

## 8. Christian Witness and Evangelism

We prepare students to share the Gospel effectively, minister across cultures, and meet spiritual needs through biblical truth and the power of the Holy Spirit.

## 9. Theology and Biblical Ethics

We equip students with sound theological understanding and biblical ethical principles to guide their personal lives, Christian leadership, and ministry responsibilities.

## 10. Servant Leadership

We develop humble, faithful, and responsible Christian leaders who demonstrate integrity, godly character, and effective leadership in the Church, family, workplace, and community.

# Our Ultimate Goal

Our goal is to prepare Christ-centered, Bible-based, and Spirit-empowered graduates who demonstrate spiritual maturity, academic excellence, servant leadership, and a lifelong commitment to fulfilling the Great Commission.
